# Next source-to-particle construction

The immediate reusable object is now one fixed-spacing, vectorlike charged
field family with a controlled local record limit and a strictly nonzero
current response. Its mass parameter m comes from the native Higgs/elementary
common source energy. That parameter is not yet the interacting particle
mass: neither a finite cube gap nor the free common cone proves that.

First close an actual charged **energy-record** experiment on the revised
cube. The free lowest charged code band is rank2, but the next level is
`sqrt(17-4sqrt3)m/2`, below `sqrt13 m/2`. Its separation from the lowest
level is only `[sqrt(17-4sqrt3)-sqrt5]m/2`, smaller than twice the frozen
all-charge perturbation bound. That bound does not isolate rank2. A sharper
fixed-charge or low/high-sector bound is needed, or a wider separated
cluster can be measured without insisting on rank2. A separately declared
completion c=23/2 can clear the native complement above the coarse lowest
energy upper bound, but cannot by itself separate the internal charged
levels. The retained outer compensator cost4 must remain in the raw clock. The
same-H finite energy-agreement/phase-estimation instruments can then read a
charged band and the neutral ground, with all preparation failures. The
rank2 band need not be called a degenerate physical spin doublet.

Next make that energy response spatial: prepare a dressed charged packet
and compare its actual energy support at several controlled momenta against
the **same coupled neutral state and clock**. The present volume theorem is
for a nonstationary free-sea preparation, so it cannot supply this stationary
state by relabeling. The extensive retained sea offset also prevents blindly
reusing the cube completion: one failed local code turns off the global
guard and pays only one completion penalty. The proved source-only option
`c(N)=18V+1` selects the code ground sector in each finite box
while retaining every raw constant. This is a new declared completion,
not an empirical mass fit; it does not yet find the coupled ground or
establish a volume-uniform internal gap. A
fresh local ground/preparation limit, or an explicitly bounded finite-window
stationary approximation, must be supplied. Uniqueness of an architecture is
not required; the chosen source and preparation are.

The charge reference must remain physical. A compensator at a finite vertex
can bind the charged excitation; subtracting its cost4 does not remove its
Coulomb interaction. A boundary-reference separation limit or a neutral
pair/dressed-correlator construction needs a quantitative reference error.
Its observable target can be a charged energy threshold at specified
infrared resolution; an isolated pole is a stronger additional claim.

Finally compare the resulting charged dispersion and photon response on one
momentum/time window. The free Gamma regulator removes the old factor-two
curvature mismatch, but the explicit vacuum compression already shows an
allowed Gamma mass correction. Only the full dressed source spectrum can
settle its physical mass and common propagation coefficient. A spacing or
low-momentum refinement must control those errors and the retained cutoff
order. No Standard Model weak chirality, generation splitting or GeV scale
is supplied by this vectorlike field or its native mass selector.
